The "Introduce Parameter Object" technique involves creating a new class or data structure to encapsulate the parameters that are passed to the function. This reduces the number of parameters in the function signature and makes the code more readable and maintainable.

### Step 3: Apply the Refactoring
We will create a new class called `NetworkParameters` to encapsulate the parameters passed to the `run` function. This class will have attributes for `input_size`, `n_actions`, `hidden_size`, and `gamma`.

